      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The test file contains one actual test method (`test_range_unsupported`) but is bloated with dozens of unused imports and nine unused data-provider methods copied from the larger test class. I'll produce a clean, focused version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports (20+ `ChronoField`/`ChronoUnit` static imports and framework imports) and the nine unused data-provider methods, leaving a focused, self-documenting test with a brief class-level Javadoc explaining *why* the exception is expected."
